# Git commits: noreply email only

## Required author / committer

- Name: `fooSynaptic`
- Email: `19420328+fooSynaptic@users.noreply.github.com`

Use env overrides on commit:

```bash
LOGIN=fooSynaptic
ID=19420328
EMAIL="${ID}+${LOGIN}@users.noreply.github.com"
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="$LOGIN" GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="$EMAIL" \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="$LOGIN" GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="$EMAIL" \
git commit -m "message here"
```

## Forbidden

- Personal inboxes in author, committer, commit message, or trailers (`@qq.com`, school/company mail, etc.)
- Putting a real mailbox in `.mailmap` as the **canonical** address (map old addresses *to* noreply)

## Checks

```bash
git log -1 --format='author: %an <%ae>%ncommitter: %cn <%ce>'
bash scripts/audit_git_authors.sh
```

Author and committer email must end with `@users.noreply.github.com`.
